              "type": "accordion",
              "items": [
                {
                  "title": "What legal considerations should I keep in mind when buying or selling a business in Ontario?",
                  "html": "<p>When engaging in the purchase or sale of a business in Ontario, it's crucial to consider factors such as contractual obligations, regulatory compliance, intellectual property rights, and potential liabilities. Consulting with a corporate lawyer is advisable to navigate these complexities.</p>"
                },
                {
                  "title": "What steps are involved in the legal process of buying a business in Toronto?",
                  "html": "<p>The legal process of buying a business in Toronto typically includes due diligence, negotiation of terms, drafting and reviewing contracts, obtaining necessary permits, and completing the transfer of assets. A business lawyer can guide you through each step.</p>"
                },
                {
                  "title": "How can I protect myself from potential liabilities when selling a business in Toronto?",
                  "html": "<p>Implementing clear contractual terms, conducting thorough due diligence, and addressing any outstanding legal issues before the sale can help minimize liabilities. A business lawyer can advise on risk mitigation strategies.</p>"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Can I use the same lawyer for both buying and selling a business transaction?",
                  "html": "<p>While it is possible for the same lawyer to represent both parties, it's generally advisable for each party to have independent legal counsel. This ensures that each party's interests are fully represented and avoids potential conflicts of interest.</p>"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
